### Additional information

From the error message it seems the `expect()` wants a function instead of a promise, but `expect(() => Promise.reject(new Error("octopus")))` also doesn't work (`Expected promise\nReceived: [Function]`).

After some more testing it seems it's `Promise.reject()` the one with a problem:

```js
// Works (notice function in the reject):
const rejecting = Promise.reject(() => new Error("octopus"));
return expect(rejecting).rejects.toThrow("octopus");

// Doesn't work (notice no function):
const rejecting = Promise.reject(new Error("octopus"));
return expect(rejecting).rejects.toThrow("octopus");
```

However [according to MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/reject), the correct syntax should be the one without the callback, not the one with the callback:

```js
Promise.reject(new Error('fail'))
```

