and this when the return/enter button is registered:
```typescript
      process.stdin.setRawMode(false);
      process.stdin.pause();
      process.stdin.off('data', listenFn);
      resolve(result); // resolves the promise - continuing the script
```


In node, this works. Both prompts allow for input to be listened to.
However, in bun, the second prompt does not receive any data if there is a pause between the prompts. If there is no pause, both receive data fine.

It appears to be related to `process.stdin.pause`/`process.stdin.resume`, as when I remove the `process.stdin.pause()` in the `stop` function, it fixes this issue. *HOWEVER*, this prevents the script from exiting when it's finished (see https://stackoverflow.com/questions/59220095/node-doesnt-exit-automatically-once-a-listener-is-set-on-stdin )

