### What is the problem this feature would solve?

`!!require('node:inspector').url()` is often used to determine the presence of inspector *and do nothing inspector-related if it is not active*

This is what OP of https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/2445 did need to make [typedoc](https://github.com/TypeStrong/typedoc) work



### What is the feature you are proposing to solve the problem?

> ### inspector.url()[#](https://nodejs.org/api/inspector.html#inspectorurl)
> Returns: [\<string>](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type) | [\<undefined>](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Undefined_type)
> Return the URL of the active inspector, or undefined if there is none.

According to documentation, returning `undefined` if there is no active inspector is correct, and as Bun doesn't have inspector implementation, the function should always return `undefined`.

https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/b0b7db5c060e830801b0273b7ff6e34e3eb5c254/src/js/node/inspector.ts#L14-L16

change to
