### What is the issue?

Clicking on "Copy as Markdown" is not working on Safari.

```
Unhandled Promise Rejection: NotAllowedError: The request is not allowed by the user agent or the platform in the current context, possibly because the user denied permission

 document.querySelectorAll(".copy-as-markdown").forEach((node) => {
        node.addEventListener("click", async () => {
            const url = node.getAttribute("data-markdown-url");
            const response = await fetch(url);
            const text = await response.text();
            await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
            node.classList.add("copy-as-markdown--copied");
            setTimeout(() => {
                node.classList.remove("copy-as-markdown--copied")
            }, 2000)
        })
    });
```

From my understanding, clipboard.writeText must be triggered during a user gesture, otherwise the promise will reject. 
Webkit seems stricter that other browser engines and doing asynchronous operations inside the click handler before using the clipboard API, will make the user gesture expire.

I've made some tests locally and removing the two await before `clipboard.writeText` fixes it, but in that case this would require to prefetch all URLS.

